    "text_full": "Thursday, May 21, 2026\nTRENDING\nSalman Khan News Today: Why the Bollywood Superstar Is Trending All Over Social Media!‘Michael’ Best Scenes: Jaafar Jackson Channels the ‘King of Pop’ Perfectly in Blockbuster Michael Jackson BiopicMouni Roy Brings Desi Royalty to Cannes 2026 in a Stunning Gujarati Patola Gown, See Pics‘Khatron Ke Khiladi 15’ Contestants Fees: Who Is Likely the Highest Paid Contestant on Rohit Shetty’s Show?Seema Singh’s Cannes 2026 Appearance With Son Shrey Singh Is All About Grace, Glamour and Indian CultureAfter ‘Mortal Kombat II’, Get ‘Mortal Kombat 3’ Update: From Storyline to Cast, All You Need to Know'Dragon' Star Jr NTR Birthday: 5 Iconic Performances That Proved He is Tollywood’s True ‘Young Tiger’‘Off Campus’ Season 2 Release Date Announced? Everything To Know About the Returning Briar University SeriesJr NTR’s ‘Dragon’ Cast, Release Date and Plot Details: An Assassin, a Cop and a Deadly Showdown Await'India's Got Latent 2' Guest Rumours: Alia Bhatt, Sharvari on Samay Raina's Show? Leaked Image Goes ViralDaily Horoscope for May 20, 2026: What Today's Astrological Predictions Reveal for Scorpio, Aquarius, Aries and MoreJr NTR's Movie ‘Dragon’ Release Date: Prashanth Neel’s High-Octane Action Spectacle Unveils Powerful First GlimpseJacqueline Fernandez Turns Heads at Cannes 2026 Chopard Miracles Gala in Elegant Vintage-Inspired Black DressPreity Zinta’s Movie ‘Vibe’ Release Date: Actor Returns To Big Screen With Kunal Kemmu’s Action-Comedy After Long HiatusBox Office Collection Report (19 May 2026): ‘Karuppu’, ‘Pati Patni Aur Woh Do’, ‘Raja Shivaji’ And More, Which Film Is Winning The Audience?\nEntertainment\nTV\nOTT\nMusic\nGlobal\nSports\nBollywood\nSouth\nHome\nEntertainment\nBollywood\nBox Office Collection Update (17 May 2026): How Much Have ‘Pati Patni Aur Woh Do’, ‘Bhooth Bangla’, ‘Raja Shivaji’ And Other Films Collected So Far?\nBox Office Collection Update (17 May 2026): How Much Have ‘Pati Patni Aur Woh Do’, ‘Bhooth Bangla’, ‘Raja Shivaji’ And Other Films Collected So Far?\nFrom ‘Pati Patni Aur Woh Do’ showing strong weekend growth to ‘Bhooth Bangla’ continuing its successful theatrical run, here’s a detailed look at the latest Bollywood box office collection update for 17 May 2026.\nRishika SinghMay 18, 2026, 10:59 IST\n\nThis weekend at the box office has been an interesting one, with a new release finding its feet while some older films continue to hold their ground. The Hindi film industry has had a packed few weeks, and the numbers from Sunday are a reflection of just how varied the audience's appetite has been. From a fresh romantic comedy generating early buzz to a horror comedy quietly nearing a major milestone, the 17 May box office update tells quite a story on its own.\n\n\n'Pati Patni Aur Woh Do' Box Office Collection Day 3\n\nMudassar Aziz's latest comic caper, starring Ayushmann Khurrana, Sara Ali Khan, Rakul Preet Singh and Vamika Gabbi, has shown healthy growth over its opening weekend. The film follows a seemingly settled couple in Prayagraj whose lives are thrown into comic disarray by one fateful decision. Day 3 saw a solid jump, and the worldwide gross now stands at Rs 24.25 crore.\n\n'Bhooth Bangla' Box Office Collection Day 31\n\nAkshay Kumar's horror comedy is refusing to slow down even on its fifth weekend. The film, which has been a consistent performer since its release, is now inching very close to the Rs 200 crore mark in India alone. Its worldwide gross has crossed Rs 253 crore, which makes it one of the stronger performers of the season.\n\n'Raja Shivaji' Box Office Collection Day 17\n\nThe Marathi historical drama has crossed Rs 100 crore in India gross, a significant milestone that underlines its consistent hold at multiplexes. Day 17 saw steady footfall with nearly 2,200 shows running across the country.\n\n'Michael' Box Office Collection Day 24\n\nMichael is a biographical drama based on the life of pop icon Michael Jackson. The film continues its run past the three-week mark, maintaining a steady presence at the box office. Its India gross currently stands at Rs 72.28 crore, with Day 24 bringing in Rs 1.90 crore across 837 shows.\n\n'Daadi Ki Shaadi' Box Office Collection Day 10\n\nThe family entertainer wrapped up its second Sunday with a worldwide gross of Rs 6.86 crore. It has been a modest but consistent run for the film, which has been playing across a wide number of shows throughout its theatrical outing.\n\nThis weekend has made it clear that audiences are turning up across genres, and the box office is in a healthy place heading into the latter half of May 2026.\n\nTRENDING\n\nSalman Khan News Today: Why the Bollywood Superstar Is Trending All Over Social Media!\n\n‘Michael’ Best Scenes: Jaafar Jackson Channels the ‘King of Pop’ Perfectly in Blockbuster Michael Jackson Biopic\n\nMouni Roy Brings Desi Royalty to Cannes 2026 in a Stunning Gujarati Patola Gown, See Pics\n\n‘Khatron Ke Khiladi 15’ Contestants Fees: Who Is Likely the Highest Paid Contestant on Rohit Shetty’s Show?\n\nSeema Singh’s Cannes 2026 Appearance With Son Shrey Singh Is All About Grace, Glamour and Indian Culture\n\nAfter ‘Mortal Kombat II’, Get ‘Mortal Kombat 3’ Update: From Storyline to Cast, All You Need to Know\n\n'Dragon' Star Jr NTR Birthday: 5 Iconic Performances That Proved He is Tollywood’s True ‘Young Tiger’\n\n‘Off Campus’ Season 2 Release Date Announced? Everything To Know About the Returning Briar University Series\n\nJr NTR’s ‘Dragon’ Cast, Release Date and Plot Details: An Assassin, a Cop and a Deadly Showdown Await\n\n'India's Got Latent 2' Guest Rumours: Alia Bhatt, Sharvari on Samay Raina's Show? Leaked Image Goes Viral\n\nDaily Horoscope for May 20, 2026: What Today's Astrological Predictions Reveal for Scorpio, Aquarius, Aries and More\n\nJr NTR's Movie ‘Dragon’ Release Date: Prashanth Neel’s High-Octane Action Spectacle Unveils Powerful First Glimpse\n\nJacqueline Fernandez Turns Heads at Cannes 2026 Chopard Miracles Gala in Elegant Vintage-Inspired Black Dress\n\nPreity Zinta’s Movie ‘Vibe’ Release Date: Actor Returns To Big Screen With Kunal Kemmu’s Action-Comedy After Long Hiatus\n\nBox Office Collection Report (19 May 2026): ‘Karuppu’, ‘Pati Patni Aur Woh Do’, ‘Raja Shivaji’ And More, Which Film Is Winning The Audience?\n\nRelated Articles\nSalman Khan News Today: Why the Bollywood Superstar Is Trending All Over Social Media!\nPreity Zinta’s Movie ‘Vibe’ Release Date: Actor Returns To Big Screen With Kunal Kemmu’s Action-Comedy After Long Hiatus\nBox Office Collection Report (19 May 2026): ‘Karuppu’, ‘Pati Patni Aur Woh Do’, ‘Raja Shivaji’ And More, Which Film Is Winning The Audience?\n‘Main Vaapas Aaunga’ Release Date Announced: Diljit Dosanjh, Vedang Raina And Sharvari Bring Imtiaz Ali’s Love Story To The Big Screen\nTerms of use Privacy Policy\nCopyright © 2026 Bennett, Coleman & Co. Ltd. All rights reserved."
